  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: "A gastronomist once wrote an article about how
    certain sauces could soften various salad ingredients, which revolutionized the
    dishes and palates of Verehnian nobles at the time. Should the gastronomist still
    be here, somehow avoiding his execution during the revolution, one can imagine
    that he would be amazed at how a parallel innovation is happening in the ramshackled
    kitchens of today. The bitter sauce and acidic, sharp cheese act in tandem to
    make the hard root vegetables turn to mush. The specific food chemistry that
    makes this possible escapes the dish\u2019s staunch fans; this does not stop
    them, though occasionally one must wonder if the viscous mixture could break
    down the vegetables, what it could do to one\u2019s stomach lining..."
